      "justification": "Given this patient's HIV/AIDS with CD4<200 and severe CAP presentation (SpO2 88%, RR 26, HR 110, hypotension), broad-spectrum coverage including atypical organisms is critical. A respiratory fluoroquinolone provides coverage for Legionella, atypical pathogens, and possible PCP prophylaxis benefit. While beta-lactam plus macrolide has been initiated, adding a fluoroquinolone or switching to fluoroquinolone monotherapy per ATS/IDSA severe CAP guidelines is appropriate for this immunocompromised patient with suspected atypical pneumonia."
    },
